DESCRIPTION >
    - `cncf_country_activity_timeseries.pipe` serves the activity-over-time chart of the CNCF country report.
    - For each period, returns the country's active contributors, contributions, and active organizations headquartered in the country.
    - Parameters:
    - `countryCode`: Required ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country code (e.g., 'FR') - inherited from `cncf_country_activities`
    - `granularity`: Required string for time aggregation ('daily', 'weekly', 'monthly', 'quarterly', 'yearly')
    - `startDate`: Required DateTime start of the series (e.g., '2024-01-01 00:00:00'); `generate_timeseries` needs it, since this pipe has no project to derive the start from
    - `endDate`: Optional DateTime end of the series (e.g., '2024-12-31 23:59:59'), defaults to now
    - `includeCodeContributions`, `includeCollaborations`, `includeOtherContributions`: Optional booleans (defaults: code contributions only)
    - Response: `startDate`, `endDate`, `contributorCount`, `contributionCount`, `organizationCount`

TOKEN "insights-app-token" READ

TAGS "Report"

NODE cncf_country_activity_timeseries_result
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        ds."startDate",
        ds."endDate",
        uniqIf(a.memberId, a.memberId != '') AS "contributorCount",
        countIf(a.memberId != '') AS "contributionCount",
        uniqIf(a.organizationId, a.organizationInCountry) AS "organizationCount"
    FROM generate_timeseries ds
    LEFT JOIN
        cncf_country_activities a
        ON CASE
            WHEN {{ granularity }} = 'daily'
            THEN toDate(a.timestamp)
            WHEN {{ granularity }} = 'weekly'
            THEN toStartOfWeek(a.timestamp)
            WHEN {{ granularity }} = 'monthly'
            THEN toStartOfMonth(a.timestamp)
            WHEN {{ granularity }} = 'quarterly'
            THEN toStartOfQuarter(a.timestamp)
            WHEN {{ granularity }} = 'yearly'
            THEN toStartOfYear(a.timestamp)
        END
        = ds."startDate"
    GROUP BY ds."startDate", ds."endDate"
    ORDER BY ds."startDate" ASC
